  "runtime": {
    "equivalence": "decision2/qwen.py loads this full checkpoint with the vendored training/model sources whose SHA-256 equal the scored adapter sources (checked at build time) and applies the per-state batching (all questions of one state in one batch), BF16-backbone / FP32-head execution, the CAL698 per-type temperatures in calibration.json and the answer normalization of training.model.infer (adapter decision2-typed with --calibration). The calibrated predictions are the scored logits divided by the temperatures: answers are identical to the uncalibrated run on every scored prompt. Checked on one GPU of the scoring node against the sealed calibrated predictions by release.sh --parity.",
